{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENLgdMcZoxLV6oZsU2g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both symptoms come from `hidden` being a DynamoDB reserved word, used bare in two kinds of expression. The fix aliases every attribute name in every expression, and a test now fails on any bare name. All 11 tests pass. The new tests fail on the original code.\n\n**Causes** (details in `ANSWER.md`)\n- **Prod crash:** `hide()` wrote `SET hidden = ...` bare in an UpdateExpression. DynamoDB rejects that with a loud `ValidationException`, which is the 500 in the log.\n- **Staging feed:** `feed()` asked for `ProjectionExpression=\"slug, title, hidden, ...\"`. A bare reserved word there is dropped silently, so the `not i.get(\"hidden\")` filter never sees the flag. Dasha's hand-hide was fine: she used `#h`, and `hidden: true` is in the table. The feed is not cached and does not read another table.\n\n**Fix** (`src/app.py`)\n- Every attribute name in `publish`, `rename`, `hide`, `feed` and `archive` is now a `#alias` with an `ExpressionAttributeNames` entry, including names that are safe today.\n- `archive()` had the same bug with `status` in a ConditionExpression. It is not wired to the API yet, so it has not crashed.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/test_feed.py`)\n- A static test parses `src/app.py` and fails on any bare attribute name in any `*Expression` string. This is what stops the bug from coming back, including the silent projection case.\n- Two feed tests set `hidden` (one through `hide()`, one the way the CLI hand-fix did) and assert the story leaves the feed. The existing tests never set the field, which is why nothing caught this.\n\n**Colleague's note:** The alias-everything rule and the \"write the field, then check the filter\" test both applied. The `similar` steps and the 573-word count did not, since this repo has neither. I could not check the real DynamoDB reserved-word list. The prod log confirms `hidden`, but `status` is confirmed only by the note and the fake's subset.\n\n**Not done**\n- No deploy and no change to staging or prod data. Once the fix ships, `my-first-week` will leave the feed, since it already has `hidden: true`.\n- The hand-hide did not set `hidden_by` or `hidden_at`. Backfilling them is a staging data change, so I left it for you to decide.\n- Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1472,"cache_read_input_tokens":49699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1472},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd166e8f-00a3-447a-bf2a-ff8085424637","uuid":"34e157aa-d885-4910-bc08-d5a556119422","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:37:30.939Z","request_id":"req_011CgENLgLjWW9L4FsXfqbo1"}
